            "notes": "[Video Link (20:20)](https://youtu.be/1uZjlqJzVTY?si=4ahOTtaAJUksRWxd&t=1220)\n\n### Power\nThe final Power for the build is [Multiball](item_5d0e4135-f4e1-42fb-991a-417643064560) to even further improve our debuff coverage. The additional orbs from Multiball are much weaker, but our extremely high Ability Power and damage boost from [Deconstruction](item_cc8c46cc-b4a3-4c0f-aeb6-f7837e0e8e7c) are doing their best to bring up the damge. \n\n### Playstyle\nThe playstyle in this round is the same as before with the added orbs from [Multiball](item_5d0e4135-f4e1-42fb-991a-417643064560). Continue firing orbs intentionally to maximize their effect. \n\n### Items\n* [Champion's Kit](item_8682f8c7-8811-439b-8d50-fa81cd43ddce) - Arx opts for maximum Ability Power because it's Quick Play, and I don't disagree. \n\n### Sell\n* [Energized Bracers](item_f83a1d9e-91f8-4d2c-bd62-c673b8d9fd2e) - Forgoing survivability and healing output for raw damage here. Alternatively, [Lum\u00e9riCo Fusion Drive](item_3da81000-333c-460a-a1a2-09441bfda9c8) or [Phantasmic Flux](item_5e644a79-cf6e-4196-8d0a-232f75004643) are decent options for still adding Ability Power while keeping some survivability.",
